>
You are carrying a trident, a metal shield and a slip of paper.
You are wearing a tunic and a skirt.
>
The slip of paper describes your task. It seems you have to steal Hades' helmet of invisibility from the throne room of his palace. Zeus also mentions that he has stripped you of your godly powers to ensure fair play.
>
The hydra is a huge serpent endowed with nine heads. She guards the entrance to the Underworld from all comers. Eight of the heads surround the vulnerable ninth, protecting it from attack. She stands between you and the gates.
>
Tranquil garden
In stark contrast with its surroundings, this idyllic garden-paradise exudes an air of peace and tranquillity. All is still, and the incongruity of the adjacent swamplands seems somehow not to matter. A rich variety of flowers thrive in the ideal climatic conditions which prevail here and a young tree stands aloof in the centre of the garden beside an imposing marble altar. The only exit is west, back to the gates. Two discarded stones lie side by side on the ground.
A small lamb frolics playfully nearby.
The lamb raises its head as you enter the garden.
>
